WEBVTT

00:11.928 --> 00:15.223
I want Units 11 through 16
to head over to West 56 District!

00:15.724 --> 00:17.392
The rest of you
are to accompany me!

00:17.559 --> 00:18.143
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

00:18.226 --> 00:20.020
Leave the bodies
of the dead for later!

00:20.186 --> 00:21.938
Transporting the injured
is our top priority!

00:22.731 --> 00:23.690
We've got a critical patient here!

00:23.773 --> 00:25.775
Please take him to room 203!

00:32.073 --> 00:33.158
Captain Unohana...

00:34.409 --> 00:35.910
was it really the right choice

00:35.994 --> 00:37.954
for us to remain in
the Squad 4 barracks?

00:38.830 --> 00:41.124
We could've saved more lives if we
were out there in the Seireitei

00:41.207 --> 00:42.876
- with the rest of—
- Isane.

00:43.793 --> 00:46.463
You shouldn't let your feelings
dictate what you say.

00:47.088 --> 00:50.550
It would have been easy for us to
vacate this place out of concern.

00:52.510 --> 00:56.306
But I know you are
not so short-sighted

00:56.389 --> 00:59.809
that I have to explain
why that would have been wrong.

01:01.561 --> 01:02.562
Yes, ma'am...

01:03.021 --> 01:05.857
I'm...very sorry...!

01:06.649 --> 01:08.985
There's no need to cry, Isane...

01:10.111 --> 01:13.531
"Do not leave the Squad 4 barracks.
No matter what."

01:14.908 --> 01:21.998
That was the final order given
to us by the Head Captain...

01:51.986 --> 01:56.783
<i>The blue skies above are hopelessly clear</i>

01:56.866 --> 02:01.955
<i>At my wit's end, I feel a growing frustration</i>

02:02.372 --> 02:06.793
<i>As if to laugh at us hopeless cowards</i>

02:07.127 --> 02:10.630
<i>Countless eyes stare at us</i>

02:11.089 --> 02:16.970
<i>This soul of mine breaks again and again</i>

02:17.262 --> 02:20.181
<i>All I can do is hold it tight</i>

02:21.391 --> 02:26.396
<i>Until the day it turns to ash</i>

02:26.646 --> 02:29.274
<i>I've absorbed all of this sorrow</i>

02:29.399 --> 02:33.903
<i>It has shaped me, painted me</i>

02:34.028 --> 02:36.739
<i>But that's how we got here, right?</i>

02:36.865 --> 02:41.703
<i>One step at a time, just like breathing</i>

02:41.828 --> 02:44.247
<i>These countless scars on my palm</i>

02:44.372 --> 02:46.249
<i>That no longer fade</i>

02:46.374 --> 02:50.003
<i>Are my badge, my story</i>

02:50.295 --> 02:53.965
<i>I faced the fear and shred it to pieces</i>

02:54.090 --> 02:57.051
<i>And let it walk beside me once more</i>

02:57.135 --> 03:02.015
BLEACH: THOUSAND-YEAR BLOOD WAR

03:14.777 --> 03:15.778
Here you go, sir.

03:16.362 --> 03:18.531
According to this message
sent by Kisuke Urahara,

03:19.032 --> 03:24.913
he, Orihime Inoue,
and Yasutora Sado are all safe.

03:25.580 --> 03:26.831
However,
further details are unknown...

03:27.582 --> 03:28.583
I see...

03:30.543 --> 03:32.003
Let me go, you idiot!

03:32.503 --> 03:33.504
The Captain...

03:33.588 --> 03:34.714
There's no way Captain Zaraki

03:34.797 --> 03:35.840
- would lose!
- Please calm down!

03:35.924 --> 03:36.925
- You need rest.
- Captain!

03:37.008 --> 03:38.384
- Get me a sedative! Hurry!
- Ichigo!

03:39.010 --> 03:41.054
Come over here, Ichigo.

03:41.387 --> 03:42.472
You need medical treatment.

03:42.847 --> 03:44.015
No, I'm fine.

03:44.432 --> 03:46.517
I already got some first-aid.

03:46.935 --> 03:47.977
No, it's not okay!

03:48.144 --> 03:51.105
I can tell that
you're badly wounded.

03:52.065 --> 03:53.066
Ichigo...

03:53.942 --> 03:56.402
Rukia and Abarai
have gotten out of surgery.

03:57.403 --> 03:58.613
TRAUMA ROOM

03:58.696 --> 03:59.197
TRAUMA ROOM

03:59.280 --> 04:00.907
They're no longer
in critical condition

04:01.366 --> 04:02.742
and are now stable.

04:03.952 --> 04:05.245
Please call me
if anything comes up.

04:09.374 --> 04:10.833
- Ichigo...
- Rukia!

04:11.084 --> 04:12.835
Is it all right for you to talk?!

04:13.670 --> 04:16.506
She just said
our condition was stable...

04:17.340 --> 04:19.592
Weren't you listening, you idiot?

04:19.759 --> 04:20.760
Oh yeah...?

04:21.052 --> 04:22.929
It seems your mouth
is working just fine...

04:24.806 --> 04:25.807
Ichigo...

04:26.849 --> 04:29.686
You came to protect
the Soul Society, didn't you?

04:30.687 --> 04:31.688
Thank you...

04:31.854 --> 04:32.772
Of course!

04:33.189 --> 04:36.401
Though,
I couldn't do anything this time...

04:36.859 --> 04:37.860
You dumbass...

04:38.152 --> 04:40.613
You drove the enemy boss away!

04:41.489 --> 04:44.784
If you hadn't come,
things would have been even worse.

04:45.827 --> 04:47.954
You should be holding
your head up high, you idiot!

04:48.913 --> 04:49.914
Hirako...

04:51.916 --> 04:53.167
Mr. Ichigo Kurosaki!

04:53.626 --> 04:55.044
Captain Kurotsuchi
would like to see you.

04:55.545 --> 04:56.754
It's about your Zanpakuto...

05:00.925 --> 05:04.679
Typical. He's always busy
no matter what the situation is.

05:05.763 --> 05:08.975
Ignoring his wounds and caring
for everybody but himself.

05:10.935 --> 05:11.936
Captain Hirako...

05:12.812 --> 05:16.899
I wonder why Ichigo had
such a painful look on his face...

05:17.567 --> 05:19.736
It seems he had
a rough time as well.

05:20.903 --> 05:22.905
His Zanpakuto was broken,

05:23.072 --> 05:25.325
and in the end,
he couldn't protect anybody.

05:25.950 --> 05:27.160
He's probably exhausted.

05:27.702 --> 05:28.953
There's no need to worry.

05:30.705 --> 05:34.417
Do you really think...that's it?

05:36.586 --> 05:38.713
I feel as if he's dealing with

05:39.839 --> 05:42.967
something more serious
and he's trying to hide it...

05:47.347 --> 05:50.350
The Head Captain's body
couldn't be found.

05:51.893 --> 05:54.395
The enemy destroyed everything...

05:57.857 --> 05:59.359
I have a report.

05:59.901 --> 06:02.612
Squad 6 Captain Byakuya Kuchiki

06:02.695 --> 06:05.740
and Squad 11 Captain
Kenpachi Zaraki

06:06.240 --> 06:07.992
have both survived.

06:08.951 --> 06:10.995
However,
it will be difficult for them

06:11.079 --> 06:12.872
to return to their duties
as captains...

06:13.498 --> 06:15.750
They may never
regain consciousness...

06:15.833 --> 06:16.834
Get out!

06:17.168 --> 06:19.253
I don't want to hear
such reports right now!

06:19.712 --> 06:22.715
Can't you see that
we lost the Head Captain?

06:23.424 --> 06:25.802
What more do you want us
to deal with?!

06:25.885 --> 06:27.595
Stop.
You're embarrassing yourself.

06:27.678 --> 06:28.930
Easy for you to say!

06:29.180 --> 06:31.808
I know you and others held a grudge
against the Head Captain!

06:31.891 --> 06:33.434
That's why you can stay so calm!

06:33.810 --> 06:35.144
How dare you...!

06:35.311 --> 06:36.687
Stop, Soi Fon!

06:37.313 --> 06:39.899
Do you think you're the only one
who wants to scream?!

06:41.484 --> 06:44.737
Now, now, now, now...

06:44.904 --> 06:46.739
No fighting.

06:47.865 --> 06:49.492
If Old Man Yama was still here,

06:49.575 --> 06:52.703
he would've lined us up
and smacked us for sure.

06:53.579 --> 06:56.624
He'd then say, "How pathetic
to see you cry and scream

06:56.707 --> 06:58.251
in front of
the articles I left behind!"

06:58.835 --> 07:00.086
Kyoraku, you bastard...

07:00.169 --> 07:01.963
The Thirteen Court Guard Squads...

07:02.839 --> 07:04.632
doesn't exist to grieve the dead

07:04.715 --> 07:07.176
or cry over the destruction
of the Soul Society.

07:08.636 --> 07:11.389
It exists to protect
the Soul Society.

07:13.141 --> 07:14.767
Let's try to look forward.

07:15.435 --> 07:17.812
We <i>are</i> the Thirteen
Court Guard Squads, aren't we?

07:19.856 --> 07:20.857
"Can't fix it"?

07:21.190 --> 07:22.191
Why not?!

07:22.733 --> 07:26.237
You fix your Zanpakuto whenever
it gets broken, don't you?!

07:26.779 --> 07:28.322
Are you stupid?

07:28.531 --> 07:30.658
I don't "fix" mine.

07:30.741 --> 07:32.743
I "modify" it.

07:33.453 --> 07:35.580
The only thing
that can fix a Zanpakuto

07:35.663 --> 07:38.624
is its owner's mind,
Spiritual Pressure,

07:38.708 --> 07:42.378
and time to infuse them
into your Zanpakuto.

07:42.670 --> 07:43.921
That's all.

07:45.715 --> 07:46.716
Fine...

07:47.008 --> 07:50.636
So you're saying I should
take it back and fix it myself.

07:51.053 --> 07:53.556
Let me finish explaining.

07:54.891 --> 07:56.809
I was only talking about Shikai.

07:56.893 --> 07:59.687
The destruction of a Zanpakuto's
Shikai and Bankai

07:59.770 --> 08:01.647
have completely different meanings.

08:02.356 --> 08:06.277
A destroyed Bankai
can <i>never</i> be restored.

08:06.694 --> 08:08.196
What?!

08:09.238 --> 08:10.865
Then what should I do?

08:13.409 --> 08:14.410
It's me.

08:18.539 --> 08:19.957
- Come back here!
- Catch him!

08:20.041 --> 08:21.501
- Kon?!
- Nooo!

08:21.584 --> 08:24.921
I hadn't seen him in a while,
but he was in the Soul Society?

08:25.880 --> 08:26.839
I see...

08:26.923 --> 08:28.174
I thought so.

08:28.841 --> 08:29.759
All right.

08:29.842 --> 08:31.093
I'm on my way.

08:32.094 --> 08:34.514
Come with me, Ichigo Kurosaki.

08:35.515 --> 08:37.308
You should meet them.

08:37.683 --> 08:40.561
Although I don't want to
in the slightest.

08:41.312 --> 08:43.731
The great Squad Zero is coming.

08:48.069 --> 08:49.070
Hirako!

08:49.820 --> 08:51.906
Came to check it out too, Ichigo?

08:52.323 --> 08:54.116
I don't really recommend it.

08:55.826 --> 08:57.954
So where's this Squad Zero
coming from?

08:58.246 --> 09:01.749
I mean, they're only showing up now
after the Seireitei got destroyed?

09:02.250 --> 09:03.834
Where do they usually stay?

09:04.418 --> 09:05.711
In the Royal Palace.

09:05.878 --> 09:08.506
Is that not within the Seireitei?

09:09.423 --> 09:11.717
Do you remember how those walls
came falling from the sky

09:11.801 --> 09:12.885
when you first came here?

09:14.595 --> 09:17.723
Those walls have been
surrounding this area

09:17.807 --> 09:20.810
since things have been chaotic
in the Seireitei lately.

09:21.060 --> 09:25.731
It was originally meant to surround
the Seireitei during emergencies.

09:26.732 --> 09:27.775
So then...

09:27.942 --> 09:30.361
If it's meant to protect
the Seireitei during emergencies,

09:30.653 --> 09:32.989
what does this wall
normally protect?

09:34.699 --> 09:35.866
Look, they're coming.

09:44.917 --> 09:45.918
What is that?!

09:46.252 --> 09:47.378
Tenchuren...

09:48.212 --> 09:50.798
It's Squad Zero's
transport vehicle.

09:51.841 --> 09:54.218
Squad Zero consists of
five total members.

09:55.511 --> 09:56.512
Just five?!

09:57.138 --> 09:58.139
They have no squad officers.

09:58.598 --> 09:59.890
All five are captains.

10:00.975 --> 10:01.976
Also...

10:02.351 --> 10:04.312
...the combined strength
of those five...

10:05.896 --> 10:08.190
...is greater than that of the entire
Thirteen Court Guard Squads.

10:35.384 --> 10:36.552
Hell yeah!

10:36.636 --> 10:39.347
We're here, we're here!
We're finally here!

10:40.806 --> 10:43.434
Squad Zero's in the house!

10:44.101 --> 10:46.937
Long time no see, you fledglings of
the Thirteen Court Guard Squads!

10:47.021 --> 10:48.564
Have you been eating right,
getting enough sleep,

10:48.648 --> 10:50.399
- and staying healthy?
- These guys are pretty different

10:50.483 --> 10:52.276
from what I had in mind...

10:53.611 --> 10:55.029
The hell was that for?!

10:55.446 --> 10:57.657
It's been a while, Shinji!

10:57.740 --> 10:59.659
Hiyori isn't with you?

10:59.909 --> 11:01.661
- How rare!
- "It's been a while"?

11:01.744 --> 11:03.245
I don't know you—

11:03.329 --> 11:05.122
Wait... "Hiyori"?

11:05.623 --> 11:07.333
Have you forgotten who I am?!

11:07.750 --> 11:09.794
It's me, Kirio!

11:09.919 --> 11:11.837
<i>Y-You're</i> Ms. Kirio?!

11:12.171 --> 11:15.132
Seriously?! You're like
a completely different person!

11:15.216 --> 11:19.303
Oh, Shinji!
I haven't changed <i>that</i> much!

11:20.513 --> 11:22.223
Ah, I'm starving!

11:26.769 --> 11:29.855
Hey! It's been a while,
hasn't it, Unohana?

11:30.523 --> 11:33.401
So, the healing techniques
I taught you...

11:33.484 --> 11:35.194
Are you putting them to good use?

11:35.361 --> 11:36.445
Of course.

11:36.612 --> 11:37.947
Really?!

11:38.197 --> 11:42.576
Because I heard you guys
just lost a bunch of men!

11:42.743 --> 11:44.704
So what's the story there?

11:46.080 --> 11:47.623
Now, now!

11:47.707 --> 11:49.625
It's been so long
since you've seen one another!

11:49.709 --> 11:51.377
I'm sure you have
a ton of catching up to do,

11:51.460 --> 11:52.586
but save it for later!

11:54.588 --> 11:55.589
Well now...

11:55.673 --> 11:59.093
I see everyone in Squad Zero
is the same as always, Osho!

11:59.802 --> 12:03.639
So what business do you have
for coming here this time?

12:04.682 --> 12:05.683
Hmm...

12:06.684 --> 12:08.686
So you're Ichigo Kurosaki, huh?

12:10.771 --> 12:13.816
We came here to rebuild
the Thirteen Court Guard Squads

12:13.899 --> 12:15.609
at the behest of the Soul King.

12:16.610 --> 12:21.657
For starters, Ichigo Kurosaki,
we're taking you back up with us.

12:22.158 --> 12:23.242
Are you kidding me?!

12:23.868 --> 12:25.953
I don't care how important
Squad Zero is,

12:26.579 --> 12:27.788
but you were relaxing above

12:27.872 --> 12:29.790
while the Seireitei
was getting destroyed.

12:30.124 --> 12:31.125
But now, you come down,

12:31.208 --> 12:32.877
wanting to rebuild
the Thirteen Court Guard Squads?!

12:33.544 --> 12:35.171
Quit joking around!

12:36.630 --> 12:38.507
Let's continue.

12:38.591 --> 12:39.717
- So...
- Hey!

12:40.551 --> 12:42.052
Shut up.

12:42.595 --> 12:44.180
<i>What kind of move was that?</i>

12:44.722 --> 12:47.224
"Quit joking around"?
That's our line.

12:47.725 --> 12:49.226
What were you again?

12:49.727 --> 12:52.188
The Thirteen Court Guard Squads.
Am I right?

12:52.730 --> 12:55.357
Our job is to protect
the Royal Palace.

12:55.733 --> 12:58.402
Your job is to protect
the Seireitei.

12:59.236 --> 13:01.655
What kind of Court Guard
cries for help

13:01.739 --> 13:04.283
after failing to get the job done?

13:04.617 --> 13:06.869
You're not worthy
to bear that name.

13:08.621 --> 13:10.372
That hurts, damn it!

13:11.832 --> 13:14.084
I told you to save it for later.

13:14.668 --> 13:17.463
Let's finish
what we came here for first.

13:17.546 --> 13:18.589
No need.

13:18.672 --> 13:19.757
Huh?

13:20.090 --> 13:22.718
Everything on the list of things
we need to take with us...

13:22.968 --> 13:24.887
They're all here.

13:28.891 --> 13:31.268
All that is remaining is you...

13:33.687 --> 13:35.064
Ichigo Kurosaki.

13:35.898 --> 13:36.982
Unacceptable.

13:37.775 --> 13:40.319
The three people
inside your spheres

13:40.402 --> 13:43.989
are in no condition to leave
the Seireitei right now.

13:44.615 --> 13:46.784
I cannot allow you
to take them with you.

13:49.954 --> 13:52.414
That's exactly why
we're taking them with us!

13:53.499 --> 13:55.334
I'm sure you're well aware

13:56.168 --> 13:59.755
that you're not strong enough
to fully restore these three.

14:01.382 --> 14:04.260
You already know, don't you, Retsu?

14:05.219 --> 14:09.682
Medical care isn't what
you should be doing right now.

14:13.352 --> 14:15.813
You broke into my lab as well, huh?

14:16.897 --> 14:20.442
As always,
you're so disrespectful.

14:21.277 --> 14:24.572
Oh, why if it isn't Mayuri.

14:24.905 --> 14:28.576
As always, you exaggerate
by calling it a break-in.

14:28.617 --> 14:32.872
When I placed my hand on the door,
it just slid right open.

14:33.831 --> 14:34.832
However...

14:35.124 --> 14:39.003
it was far less secure
than when I was around.

14:40.796 --> 14:42.256
H-Hold on a second!

14:42.798 --> 14:44.341
Why are you taking me as well?!

14:44.800 --> 14:48.178
I can recover from these injuries
just fine in the Seireitei!

14:50.139 --> 14:51.390
We know that.

14:51.599 --> 14:54.810
You're the only one being taken
for a different reason.

14:55.436 --> 14:56.645
"A different reason"?

14:56.979 --> 14:58.606
<i>Hello there!</i>

14:58.939 --> 15:01.734
<i>Well, it's been a while</i>
<i>since I've seen you all!</i>

15:01.901 --> 15:03.277
<i>I'm sure you must have</i>
<i>been worried.</i>

15:03.819 --> 15:05.738
<i>I'm so sorry about that.</i>

15:06.405 --> 15:07.406
<i>Huh?</i>

15:07.615 --> 15:10.868
<i>Hey, what gives?</i>
<i>I was hoping for a bigger reaction.</i>

15:12.661 --> 15:13.787
What's going on here?!

15:14.038 --> 15:16.832
- My head!
- <i>Oh! It's Kurosaki!</i>

15:17.541 --> 15:19.376
<i>Thank goodness!</i>

15:19.585 --> 15:21.462
<i>You're hurt,</i>
<i>but you look all right!</i>

15:21.712 --> 15:23.464
Inoue!
Thank goodness!

15:23.714 --> 15:24.632
You seem to be doing well!

15:25.174 --> 15:27.176
<i>Yeah, I'm all right!</i>

15:28.719 --> 15:29.762
<i>That you, Ichigo?</i>

15:29.845 --> 15:32.139
<i>Thank goodness you're safe.</i>

15:32.640 --> 15:36.435
That's my line.
I was worried too, you know.

15:36.769 --> 15:41.023
<i>Well, the truth is,</i>
<i>I wanted to contact you sooner,</i>

15:41.106 --> 15:42.608
<i>but a lot happened...</i>

15:42.858 --> 15:44.860
<i>Huh?</i>
<i>What are you guys doing in there?</i>

15:46.779 --> 15:48.238
That voice...
Could it be?

15:49.114 --> 15:51.617
- <i>That voice!</i>
- <i>Inoue! Sado!</i>

15:51.742 --> 15:52.618
<i>Kurosaki, you bastard!</i>

15:52.826 --> 15:54.244
<i>You're there, aren't you?!</i>

15:54.328 --> 15:55.621
- <i>No!</i>
- <i>Hey, why are you</i>

15:55.704 --> 15:57.456
- <i>He's not here!</i>
- <i>with that guy, Urahara?!</i>

15:57.581 --> 15:58.582
<i>Kurosaki...</i>

15:59.625 --> 16:02.670
As you can see,
we're all right.

16:03.295 --> 16:05.798
So please do what you have to do
for yourself...

16:06.632 --> 16:12.304
You can decide on your own...
what you truly want to do...

16:15.432 --> 16:18.060
<i>Oh, and don't worry about him.</i>

16:18.769 --> 16:20.896
<i>We reached a nice agreement.</i>

16:21.355 --> 16:22.648
<i>Well, see you later!</i>

16:25.901 --> 16:28.445
Was it okay to tell him that?

16:28.821 --> 16:30.114
Tell him what?

16:33.367 --> 16:37.705
If he does
what he truly wants to do...

16:38.372 --> 16:42.793
that will surely lead to
protecting us all in the end.

16:43.335 --> 16:47.798
But you two should know that
better than I do.

16:49.591 --> 16:50.718
And the person...

16:51.719 --> 16:56.015
who knows that better than anyone
is Kurosaki himself.

16:57.683 --> 16:58.767
Hey, Baldy...

16:59.101 --> 17:00.686
Oh!
You're talking to me?!

17:01.520 --> 17:05.899
If I go to this Royal Palace,
can I fix my Tensa Zangetsu?

17:06.775 --> 17:08.235
That's impossible.

17:08.318 --> 17:09.737
It can't be fixed.

17:10.696 --> 17:11.697
However...

17:11.864 --> 17:13.741
if you go to the Royal Palace,

17:13.824 --> 17:17.703
we can reforge it into something
resembling your original sword.

17:21.623 --> 17:22.624
Fine...

17:24.710 --> 17:26.712
Take me with you
to the Royal Palace!

17:28.589 --> 17:29.214
All right!

17:29.298 --> 17:31.300
"WELCOME TO
KUKAKU SHIBA'S RESIDENCE"

17:31.759 --> 17:32.760
Huh?

17:34.011 --> 17:35.763
Go!

17:39.683 --> 17:42.269
Aren't there any seatbelts
in this thing?!

17:43.812 --> 17:44.688
There he goes.

17:45.272 --> 17:47.149
You sure it was
the right thing to do, Sis?!

17:48.025 --> 17:49.026
Yeah.

17:49.610 --> 17:51.028
If he doesn't go now,

17:51.320 --> 17:53.864
the Soul Society is finished
when the next invasion comes.

17:55.407 --> 17:57.117
We have no choice
but to let him go.

17:58.786 --> 18:02.831
Even if that means
making Uncle sad.

18:05.709 --> 18:07.086
All right, you guys!

18:07.169 --> 18:09.546
Get back to Kukaku's
Great Training Hall already!

18:09.922 --> 18:11.965
Help out with the training!

18:12.216 --> 18:15.719
Don't forget who took you off
the streets of the Rukon District.

18:16.678 --> 18:18.806
I'm getting tired of
her patronizing attitude...

18:18.889 --> 18:20.432
Agreed.

18:21.433 --> 18:22.726
Show some guts, Ganju.

18:23.602 --> 18:26.980
You can cry or scream, but I'm
throwing you into the next battle!

18:28.398 --> 18:29.399
Got it!

18:34.488 --> 18:36.281
Come on out, Ichigo Kurosaki!

18:37.699 --> 18:38.742
We've arrived!

18:38.992 --> 18:39.618
THE ROYAL PALACE

18:39.701 --> 18:41.787
THE ROYAL PALACE

18:41.870 --> 18:43.956
THE ROYAL PALACE

18:50.712 --> 18:51.713
This is the place?

18:51.797 --> 18:52.589
That's right!

18:53.132 --> 18:54.258
Feel free to brag about it!

18:54.591 --> 18:58.929
Ordinary Soul Reapers
typically aren't allowed here!

18:59.847 --> 19:04.518
Though, I'm not sure if I can
call you an "ordinary" Soul Reaper...

19:05.102 --> 19:08.689
<i>So this is the place Aizen</i>
<i>so desperately wanted to come to...</i>

19:10.440 --> 19:11.441
Hold on a second!

19:11.650 --> 19:15.195
I thought you couldn't get into
the Royal Palace without the Ouken!

19:15.529 --> 19:17.281
Yeah, this is it.

19:17.865 --> 19:20.200
The Ouken refers to our bones,

19:20.242 --> 19:23.537
which were transformed
by the power of the Soul King

19:23.620 --> 19:26.790
when we were selected
to join Squad Zero.

19:27.249 --> 19:30.294
Therefore, there are two ways
to enter the Royal Palace...

19:30.711 --> 19:35.841
We either choose to allow you in
or you come in with us...

19:36.758 --> 19:39.553
Sosuke Aizen was
trying to make an Ouken.

19:39.636 --> 19:40.637
In other words...

19:41.138 --> 19:46.101
he was trying to create us
using his own spiritual powers.

19:46.977 --> 19:49.813
He schemed to
take the place of a god...

19:50.147 --> 19:53.400
by creating life
and killing the king...

19:55.527 --> 19:56.904
Sosuke Aizen...

19:57.571 --> 20:00.282
He truly is evil personified.

20:01.450 --> 20:04.119
But take this to heart,
Ichigo Kurosaki.

20:05.454 --> 20:07.664
The Quincies
that showed up this time

20:07.748 --> 20:10.209
are an even greater evil...

20:13.962 --> 20:16.548
All right.
Stand right there!

20:16.757 --> 20:18.508
Ready?
I'm about to blast you now.

20:18.592 --> 20:20.761
Don't move, or you'll die!

20:21.345 --> 20:22.888
Okay, here goes...!

20:23.096 --> 20:24.723
H-Hold on a second!

20:24.806 --> 20:27.267
- What is it?
- Where am I heading to?!

20:27.559 --> 20:28.936
Am I going to meet the Soul King?!

20:29.478 --> 20:31.939
Huh? Are you talking in your sleep
or something?!

20:32.064 --> 20:35.192
There's no way you'd be allowed
to meet the Soul King!

20:35.525 --> 20:37.694
- That hurts, damn it!
- Explain it to him properly!

20:37.778 --> 20:39.238
THE ROYAL PALACE - MAIN ENTRANCE

20:39.321 --> 20:41.448
THE ROYAL PALACE - MAIN ENTRANCE

20:41.531 --> 20:45.285
REIO GREATER PALACE

20:45.369 --> 20:47.621
REIO GREATER PALACE

20:47.704 --> 20:48.205
REIO GREATER PALACE

20:48.288 --> 20:52.042
SQUAD ZERO RIDEN

20:52.125 --> 20:53.877
SQUAD ZERO RIDEN

20:53.961 --> 20:55.754
SQUAD ZERO RIDEN

20:55.879 --> 20:58.465
Out of those...

20:58.924 --> 21:03.971
you'll be first going to
my Kirinden—all of you!

21:05.806 --> 21:06.807
"KIRINDEN"

21:10.018 --> 21:11.270
What the hell is this?!

21:11.728 --> 21:14.439
We're soaking in a hot spring,
of course.

21:14.523 --> 21:15.691
Why are you drowning them?!

21:15.774 --> 21:16.775
You're going to kill them!

21:17.150 --> 21:18.694
Wait!
He's bleeding!

21:18.902 --> 21:20.779
Quit your yapping.

21:21.321 --> 21:23.657
I'm soaking them in this hot water
to squeeze out

21:23.740 --> 21:25.784
their damaged Spiritual Pressure
along with their blood.

21:26.368 --> 21:27.911
Damaged Spiritual Pressure?

21:28.370 --> 21:30.622
You see that red hot spring
over there?

21:31.581 --> 21:32.082
"BLOOD POND HELL"

21:32.165 --> 21:33.834
"BLOOD POND HELL"

21:33.917 --> 21:36.086
"BLOOD POND HELL"

21:36.545 --> 21:40.590
We're going to take Byakuya,
who's completely squeezed out...

21:40.757 --> 21:42.092
and toss him in there!

21:42.759 --> 21:44.803
Hey!
He's on the verge of death!

21:44.845 --> 21:46.680
I told you to shut up!

21:47.222 --> 21:49.683
I draw out their blood
in White Bone Hell

21:49.766 --> 21:51.893
and replenish it
in Blood Pond Hell.

21:52.352 --> 21:54.146
I'll repeat this several times,

21:54.646 --> 21:57.858
and in the end, every drop of
bad blood and Spiritual Pressure

21:57.941 --> 22:00.777
in their bodies
will be swapped with my hot water!

22:01.278 --> 22:03.238
That's the way I heal others!

22:03.780 --> 22:05.699
Will doing this really work?

22:05.782 --> 22:07.242
Shut up and soak.

22:07.617 --> 22:09.369
With the kind of injuries you have,

22:10.495 --> 22:14.583
one night is enough to make you
feel twice as good as normal!

22:14.666 --> 22:16.752
"HOT SPRING DEMON" -
TENJIRO KIRINJI

22:24.259 --> 22:27.262
<i>Everything we had left behind</i>

22:27.429 --> 22:31.558
<i>Our breaths blending as mist</i>

22:31.641 --> 22:36.063
<i>without form or expression</i>

22:36.188 --> 22:40.359
<i>We lie buried as we glare</i>
<i>into the distance</i>

22:40.692 --> 22:43.320
<i>I can't hear anything</i>

22:43.445 --> 22:46.573
<i>I can't seem to cut anything</i>

22:46.698 --> 22:49.076
<i>It feels like I'm sinking</i>

22:49.201 --> 22:50.994
<i>Falling, falling</i>

22:51.119 --> 22:52.079
<i>Touching</i>

22:52.204 --> 22:55.582
<i>Eyes struck wide open</i>

22:55.665 --> 22:58.919
<i>Something no one has ever seen</i>

22:59.044 --> 23:05.217
<i>The furthest reaches are now visible to us</i>

23:05.592 --> 23:09.221
<i>It cannot be undone</i>
<i>and cannot be stopped</i>

23:09.346 --> 23:12.682
<i>This ensuing struggle</i>

23:12.766 --> 23:17.479
<i>Whisk it away beyond</i>
<i>the ends of the earth</i>

23:17.604 --> 23:19.648
<i>Along with our breaths</i>

23:19.856 --> 23:21.149
<i>Take everything</i>

23:21.233 --> 23:25.987
<i>Whisk it away beyond</i>
<i>the ends of the earth</i>

23:26.113 --> 23:28.031
<i>Along with our futures</i>

23:28.156 --> 23:29.908
<i>Along with our world</i>

23:30.992 --> 23:34.204
<i>Something no one has ever seen</i>

23:34.329 --> 23:40.585
<i>The furthest reaches are now</i>
<i>visible to us</i>

23:40.669 --> 23:42.671
<i>Don't you know God's demand?</i>

23:42.796 --> 23:44.589
<i>Don't you know God's demand?</i>

23:44.714 --> 23:48.093
<i>As we tear each other down</i>

23:58.645 --> 24:00.522
It seems you're awake...

24:01.273 --> 24:02.482
Soul King.

24:11.491 --> 24:14.244
<i>"Neither form nor soul</i>
<i>shall escape my blade..."</i>

24:16.413 --> 24:19.416
<i>"Nothing...except you."</i>
